
> “Have you ever heard of quantum entanglement?
(giggle) It sounds mysterious, doesn’t it?

Imagine two tiny particles that become best friends — linked in a special way.
No matter how far apart they are, when you change one, the other reacts instantly!

Even if one is here on Earth and the other is across the galaxy — boom — they’re still connected!

Einstein called it ‘spooky action at a distance.’

Today, scientists are using this strange connection to build quantum computers and super-secure communication systems.

(light laugh) The quantum world may be weird… but it’s shaping the future in ways we’re only beginning to imagine.”
